(2473281, 340284, 49716, '<td valign="top">I''m not a big fan of pet shots, but this one is very well done.  I''m sure it will go down well with DPC voters.<br/> <br/>It would have been even beter without the collar I think.</td>', 'I''m not a big fan of pet shots, but this one is very well done.  I''m sure it will go down well with DPC voters. It would have been even beter without the collar I think.', '2006-05-31 19:08:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473284, 340350, 6999, '<td valign="top">Interesting object - I''m afraid not terribly interestingly shot. Filling the frmae certainly adds a little impact, but the light on the object is very flat indeed - distinguishing the teeth is nearly impossible - and perhaps some sense of environment would help - something for it actually to be protecting? Technical stuff is fine, but not enough alone.</td>', 'Interesting object - I''m afraid not terribly interestingly shot. Filling the frmae certainly adds a little impact, but the light on the object is very flat indeed - distinguishing the teeth is nearly impossible - and perhaps some sense of environment would help - something for it actually to be protecting? Technical stuff is fine, but not enough alone.', '2006-05-31 19:09:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473285, 340724, 52675, '<td valign="top">This is great. I love the pink socks! AND I''m glad he''s wearing a towel.</td>', 'This is great. I love the pink socks! AND I''m glad he''s wearing a towel.', '2006-05-31 19:10:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473286, 340289, 6999, '<td valign="top">I think you''ve overdone it on the pills, so to speak. It robs this image of any sense of realism, for which it would seem to depend for its impact; so it becomes just a cod pose, and possibly slightly dismissive of the idea of despair, by implication.</td>', 'I think you''ve overdone it on the pills, so to speak. It robs this image of any sense of realism, for which it would seem to depend for its impact; so it becomes just a cod pose, and possibly slightly dismissive of the idea of despair, by implication.', '2006-05-31 19:12:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473295, 340775, 6999, '<td valign="top">Nature? Don''t see that at all - I see a child of chemically enhanced toys, clothes printing and fabrics. Nice family portrait though - has character.</td>', 'Nature? Don''t see that at all - I see a child of chemically enhanced toys, clothes printing and fabrics. Nice family portrait though - has character.', '2006-05-31 19:17:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473300, 340308, 6999, '<td valign="top">Made me smile, so points to you. It''s the position of his/her arms that does it - clever photography. Perhaps a touch fierce on the sharpening, but who cares that much? (well, the technical obsessives might ...)</td>', 'Made me smile, so points to you. It''s the position of his/her arms that does it - clever photography. Perhaps a touch fierce on the sharpening, but who cares that much? (well, the technical obsessives might ...)', '2006-05-31 19:21:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473312, 339156, 6999, '<td valign="top">Like this - her odrinary non-ordinariness is intriguing. Theres''s a mystery to that bag, too.</td>', 'Like this - her odrinary non-ordinariness is intriguing. Theres''s a mystery to that bag, too.', '2006-05-31 19:25:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473315, 338910, 52675, '<td valign="top">I can see your idea with this, but think a little more light on the person would have helped.  Just too dark.</td>', 'I can see your idea with this, but think a little more light on the person would have helped.  Just too dark.', '2006-05-31 19:25:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473318, 340487, 6999, '<td valign="top">Certainly gives <i>me</i> that feeling. Thanks for making me smile.</td>', 'Certainly gives me that feeling. Thanks for making me smile.', '2006-05-31 19:26:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473323, 340792, 9906, '<td valign="top">For a set up shot like this to truly work, it has to be damn near perfect.  You are close here but have lost a lot of the detail in your ice either through over exposure or in your pp.  I think it may be an exposure problem looking at the hot reflections on the bottle.<br/>TC</td>', 'For a set up shot like this to truly work, it has to be damn near perfect.  You are close here but have lost a lot of the detail in your ice either through over exposure or in your pp.  I think it may be an exposure problem looking at the hot reflections on the bottle.TC', '2006-05-31 19:27:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473329, 340560, 9906, '<td valign="top">What an interesting looking event.  Looks like a great time!  Your shot here is a touch out of focus and is very busy.  You may have had better luck moving around and trying to isolate 2 or 3 of the performers.  It''s also a very hard time of day to shoot with the lighting so strong.  Too much contrast.<br/>TC</td>', 'What an interesting looking event.  Looks like a great time!  Your shot here is a touch out of focus and is very busy.  You may have had better luck moving around and trying to isolate 2 or 3 of the performers.  It''s also a very hard time of day to shoot with the lighting so strong.  Too much contrast.TC', '2006-05-31 19:29:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473333, 340620, 6999, '<td valign="top">So many Eleanor lines here ... I can''t decide about this - pretentious, or quite sweet?</td>', 'So many Eleanor lines here ... I can''t decide about this - pretentious, or quite sweet?', '2006-05-31 19:29:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473336, 340496, 41033, '<td valign="top">Great silouhuette</td>', 'Great silouhuette', '2006-05-31 19:30:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473343, 340143, 9906, '<td valign="top">For me this is a touch underexposed.  I would rather see more of the detail in the foreground.  You can accomplish this with bracketing either in camera or if you shoot raw in the raw converter.  You can then combine the two images to have all the cool sky detail and brighter foreground.  This also suffers from not having a subject.  It''s nice and all, but doesn''t hold a lot of attention after the initial ''wow that''s nice and all''...<br/>TC</td>', 'For me this is a touch underexposed.  I would rather see more of the detail in the foreground.  You can accomplish this with bracketing either in camera or if you shoot raw in the raw converter.  You can then combine the two images to have all the cool sky detail and brighter foreground.  This also suffers from not having a subject.  It''s nice and all, but doesn''t hold a lot of attention after the initial ''wow that''s nice and all''...TC', '2006-05-31 19:31:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473347, 340294, 49804, '<td valign="top">10- wow, that is one of the most amazing shots ive ever seen, goes on favorites list</td>', '10- wow, that is one of the most amazing shots ive ever seen, goes on favorites list', '2006-05-31 19:32:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473351, 340570, 6999, '<td valign="top">Whoa, strange electric baby. Kind of fun shot, though i think i would personally have been unhappy with that half-cropped eye. Knockout light though.</td>', 'Whoa, strange electric baby. Kind of fun shot, though i think i would personally have been unhappy with that half-cropped eye. Knockout light though.', '2006-05-31 19:33:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473355, 340449, 6999, '<td valign="top">Nice portrait, if only you''d kept those highlights more under control. I get more of a sense of detail around her arm than her face, which is a shame also.</td>', 'Nice portrait, if only you''d kept those highlights more under control. I get more of a sense of detail around her arm than her face, which is a shame also.', '2006-05-31 19:34:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473356, 340352, 41033, '<td valign="top">Beautiful photo, beautiful flower</td>', 'Beautiful photo, beautiful flower', '2006-05-31 19:35:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473358, 340736, 27605, '<td valign="top">Best I''ve seen for this title yet.  The shy, tentative feeling is conveyed extremely well.  Even better IMO if the hands were sharper.  (7)</td>', 'Best I''ve seen for this title yet.  The shy, tentative feeling is conveyed extremely well.  Even better IMO if the hands were sharper.  (7)', '2006-05-31 19:35:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473362, 340289, 9906, '<td valign="top">Not sure I like the vignetting but other wise a very emotional shot!<br/>TC</td>', 'Not sure I like the vignetting but other wise a very emotional shot!TC', '2006-05-31 19:36:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473389, 340697, 47483, '<td valign="top">Man, this was real good.</td>', 'Man, this was real good.', '2006-05-31 19:44:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473397, 338791, 52675, '<td valign="top">Nice capture.</td>', 'Nice capture.', '2006-05-31 19:47:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473420, 340303, 48577, '<td valign="top">She''s sooooo beautiful!</td>', 'She''s sooooo beautiful!', '2006-05-31 19:52:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473424, 340209, 59194, '<td valign="top">Great composition!  The stripes draw my eyes to his face and back up again.</td>', 'Great composition!  The stripes draw my eyes to his face and back up again.', '2006-05-31 19:53:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473425, 339936, 48577, '<td valign="top">Strong colours!</td>', 'Strong colours!', '2006-05-31 19:53:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473427, 340737, 48577, '<td valign="top">Great mood.</td>', 'Great mood.', '2006-05-31 19:54:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473430, 339447, 48577, '<td valign="top">A bit dark, I think... But good.</td>', 'A bit dark, I think... But good.', '2006-05-31 19:54:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473437, 340617, 48577, '<td valign="top">Beautiful lighting.</td>', 'Beautiful lighting.', '2006-05-31 19:55:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473487, 340554, 52675, '<td valign="top">Nice green apple.  I bet you wish you had saved this for the "Green" challenge.</td>', 'Nice green apple.  I bet you wish you had saved this for the "Green" challenge.', '2006-05-31 20:01:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2473498, 340780, 37719, '<td valign="top">Courtesy critique:<br/> <br/>Composition/perspective:  The overall balance and composition is good in the image.  The subject is well placed for the crop - eliminates thirds as a negative.  The apparent weight of the statue (appears to be solid metal which indicates weight) with the stone wall behind it creates a presence that should install a sense of strength and permanence.  The problem with that perspective, IMO, is the focus and light (see below).  The DoF presented in the shot is a little confusing - perhaps the processing?  The statue is crisp and sharp, the pillars appear soft with the detail sort of blurred, but the stone wall behind, although blurred as if DoF is the controlling factor, but the edges are a bit too sharp to support that m- as in the pillar seems to be more out of focus than the wall does.<br/> <br/>Color: The preservation of such harsh...or cold colors is well done.  The tonal range is well preserved.  Some of the white appears a bit bright (see below), but the preservation of the rich metallic feel of the statue and the hard delineation of the stone wall is well done.  The splash of blue I find refreshing in the shot - the calm or eye of the storm so to speak.<br/> <br/>Light:  I find this aspect to be not as strong as the others.  The pillar appears a bit bright, as does the header beam above the words.  The top of the statue''s head is lost in the beam as well as the shoulder (his right, picture left).  This spot seems to draw attention due to this.  The highlights on the arms are not as distracting as there is more definition in shape whereas the head appears to be flat because of it..<br/> <br/>Challenge requirements:  this is where I feel it fell short.  The words above the statue are from French Legion and actually mean "Honor and Fatherland.''  This is a total disconnect from the mood and lyric of the song. The song is indicative of someone going it alone without the help/companionship of another after the break-up of a relationship and the photo indicates something of honor or patriotism in times of battle.  It may have come across stronger without the words in the shot.  Then it would be a solitary person with no outside reference to influence the voters.  The one element of the lyric that is represented well here is individual strength.  But I don''t think most voters will go that far...they will take it on first impression from a very short look.<br/> <br/>Overall/my opinion:  I will admit I am not that familiar with the Beatles and their music.  I did a lot of research for this challenge.  This was one song I had to look up.  I really like the intent of the shot and the strength of the presence of the statue in the composition.  But feel that was offset by the text.  It just changes the whole mood of the shot from a lyric to more of a remembrance or tribute/memorial.  Without that I think it would be much stronger for the purpose.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps, please feel free to PM to discuss any element above.<br/> <br/>C/A</td>', 'Courtesy critique: Composition/perspective:  The overall balance and composition is good in the image.  The subject is well placed for the crop - eliminates thirds as a negative.  The apparent weight of the statue (appears to be solid metal which indicates weight) with the stone wall behind it creates a presence that should install a sense of strength and permanence.  The problem with that perspective, IMO, is the focus and light (see below).  The DoF presented in the shot is a little confusing - perhaps the processing?  The statue is crisp and sharp, the pillars appear soft with the detail sort of blurred, but the stone wall behind, although blurred as if DoF is the controlling factor, but the edges are a bit too sharp to support that m- as in the pillar seems to be more out of focus than the wall does. Color: The preservation of such harsh...or cold colors is well done.  The tonal range is well preserved.  Some of the white appears a bit bright (see below), but the preservation of the rich metallic feel of the statue and the hard delineation of the stone wall is well done.  The splash of blue I find refreshing in the shot - the calm or eye of the storm so to speak. Light:  I find this aspect to be not as strong as the others.  The pillar appears a bit bright, as does the header beam above the words.  The top of the statue''s head is lost in the beam as well as the shoulder (his right, picture left).  This spot seems to draw attention due to this.  The highlights on the arms are not as distracting as there is more definition in shape whereas the head appears to be flat because of it.. Challenge requirements:  this is where I feel it fell short.  The words above the statue are from French Legion and actually mean "Honor and Fatherland.''  This is a total disconnect from the mood and lyric of the song. The song is indicative of someone going it alone without the help/companionship of another after the break-up of a relationship and the photo indicates something of honor or patriotism in times of battle.  It may have come across stronger without the words in the shot.  Then it would be a solitary person with no outside reference to influence the voters.  The one element of the lyric that is represented well here is individual strength.  But I don''t think most voters will go that far...they will take it on first impression from a very short look. Overall/my opinion:  I will admit I am not that familiar with the Beatles and their music.  I did a lot of research for this challenge.  This was one song I had to look up.  I really like the intent of the shot and the strength of the presence of the statue in the composition.  But feel that was offset by the text.  It just changes the whole mood of the shot from a lyric to more of a remembrance or tribute/memorial.  Without that I think it would be much stronger for the purpose. Hope this helps, please feel free to PM to discuss any element above. C/A', '2006-05-31 20:03:52.000000', NULL, 1),
