(2495209, 340445, 14414, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pamelasue:</b></div><hr/><i> what an amazing capture ... how long did you have to sit there to get just the right shot?! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Wish I could say I put hours of patience but to be honest I just got lucky. He was in a meadow just the other side of a canal I was walking along - so waited less than 5 minutes to get him stood up like that, peeking over the grass.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by TheStick:</b></div><hr/><i> Question - Is it real or stuffed? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Real, honest :)<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by lynnesite:</b></div><hr/><i> Looks a lot wider than 70mm!  </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>How about 210mm? ;) Shot at the longest end of my lens, thats like 420mm in 35mm equivalent. Looks narrow to me, but I guess that''s ''cause I was there - maybe the crop makes it appear wider...</td>', 'Originally posted by pamelasue: what an amazing capture ... how long did you have to sit there to get just the right shot?!   Wish I could say I put hours of patience but to be honest I just got lucky. He was in a meadow just the other side of a canal I was walking along - so waited less than 5 minutes to get him stood up like that, peeking over the grass. Originally posted by TheStick: Question - Is it real or stuffed?   Real, honest :) Originally posted by lynnesite: Looks a lot wider than 70mm!    How about 210mm? ;) Shot at the longest end of my lens, thats like 420mm in 35mm equivalent. Looks narrow to me, but I guess that''s ''cause I was there - maybe the crop makes it appear wider...', '2006-06-07 15:34:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2495215, 340450, 3214, '<td valign="top">Nice setup!  The depth of field needed to be wider, in my opinion, so rocky''s head wouldn''t be fuzzy.</td>', 'Nice setup!  The depth of field needed to be wider, in my opinion, so rocky''s head wouldn''t be fuzzy.', '2006-06-07 15:37:28.000000', NULL, 0),
