(2496554, 340534, 39057, '<td valign="top">This should be Blue.</td>', 'This should be Blue.', '2006-06-07 21:54:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496559, 338709, 5885, '<td valign="top"><b><i>::: Greetings from Critique Club :::</i></b> <br/> <br/>Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression - the most important one:</b> <br/>Nice warm shot fits the title and challenge well.<br/> <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>I''m not that educated with landscape type shots, but I think yoou could have strengthened this composition a bit by excluding some of the dark space at the top of the photo and moving the sun a little further left in the composition.<br/> <br/><b>Technical (Color, focus, and light):</b> <br/>Color: Warm feeling and I like it.<br/>Focus seems good.<br/>I love the light play in this image. Good work.<br/> <br/><b>To grow its vote?:</b> <br/>More dramatic post processing could have helped some. Also, strengthening the composition would have helped.<br/> <br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>I really like this shot, very warm and inviting.<br/> <br/>Hope to see more from you soon,<br/>Leroy</td>', '::: Greetings from Critique Club :::  Hi, as requested, here is an indepth critique of your submission. First Impression - the most important one: Nice warm shot fits the title and challenge well. Composition: I''m not that educated with landscape type shots, but I think yoou could have strengthened this composition a bit by excluding some of the dark space at the top of the photo and moving the sun a little further left in the composition. Technical (Color, focus, and light): Color: Warm feeling and I like it.Focus seems good.I love the light play in this image. Good work. To grow its vote?: More dramatic post processing could have helped some. Also, strengthening the composition would have helped. Summary: I really like this shot, very warm and inviting. Hope to see more from you soon,Leroy', '2006-06-07 21:55:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496566, 340651, 29490, '<td valign="top">Very nice cindi, even bitter-JP voted high for love :)<br/> <br/>I thought this would do better.  Voters - sheesh.</td>', 'Very nice cindi, even bitter-JP voted high for love :) I thought this would do better.  Voters - sheesh.', '2006-06-07 21:57:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496578, 340045, 49672, '<td valign="top">IR rocks, and that''s a great usage of it.</td>', 'IR rocks, and that''s a great usage of it.', '2006-06-07 22:00:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496590, 338791, 39057, '<td valign="top">Perfect butterfly shot! Should have placed higher.</td>', 'Perfect butterfly shot! Should have placed higher.', '2006-06-07 22:04:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496594, 340697, 39057, '<td valign="top">Fine capture. You don''t get a chance to find these kinds of shots often. Good Job.</td>', 'Fine capture. You don''t get a chance to find these kinds of shots often. Good Job.', '2006-06-07 22:06:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496603, 340573, 21816, '<td valign="top"><b>* Greetings from the Critique Club *</b> <br/> <br/>This is a great idea for the challenge IMO. The subjects marching in unison sits well with your title. So what went wrong in terms of the voting?<br/> <br/>The main thing that hits me is that the photo doesn''t really pop out at me. Maybe working with your contrasting a little more may of helped that. You should of hit it a little more with the levels adjustment layer. <br/> <br/>The other thing that really stands out to me is that the focus is a little soft. Maybe even having used a bigger DOF may of helped get all those feet in focus across the entire photo?<br/> <br/>I think the crop you have used is fine. You stated that you needed to help with a cluttered background so you have done the right thing here to make it fit the challenge.<br/> <br/>All up, I think the photo just lacked that bit of ''oompf'' to help win the voters over a bit more and that is why it finished where it did. Keep at it and best of luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Neil</td>', '* Greetings from the Critique Club *  This is a great idea for the challenge IMO. The subjects marching in unison sits well with your title. So what went wrong in terms of the voting? The main thing that hits me is that the photo doesn''t really pop out at me. Maybe working with your contrasting a little more may of helped that. You should of hit it a little more with the levels adjustment layer.  The other thing that really stands out to me is that the focus is a little soft. Maybe even having used a bigger DOF may of helped get all those feet in focus across the entire photo? I think the crop you have used is fine. You stated that you needed to help with a cluttered background so you have done the right thing here to make it fit the challenge. All up, I think the photo just lacked that bit of ''oompf'' to help win the voters over a bit more and that is why it finished where it did. Keep at it and best of luck in future challenges. Neil', '2006-06-07 22:08:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496635, 339857, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>  A new PB! Great shot too. I love the open beaks. The color is excellent. Except for the bright flash, which you noted, I don''t really see anything that could be improved. And you didn''t even get a single one! Way to go!</td>', 'Trading post...  A new PB! Great shot too. I love the open beaks. The color is excellent. Except for the bright flash, which you noted, I don''t really see anything that could be improved. And you didn''t even get a single one! Way to go!', '2006-06-07 22:19:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496714, 340294, 27164, '<td valign="top">Wow, simply a breathtaking landscape!  Going in my favorites.  Congrats on your yellow ribbon.</td>', 'Wow, simply a breathtaking landscape!  Going in my favorites.  Congrats on your yellow ribbon.', '2006-06-07 22:29:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496722, 340496, 27164, '<td valign="top">I love the colors in the sky and the strong sillhouette.</td>', 'I love the colors in the sky and the strong sillhouette.', '2006-06-07 22:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496725, 340445, 11854, '<td valign="top">Trading post...<br/>  Congratulations on your top ten finish! This is an excellent shot and your processing is fantastic. I love how the rabbit is so sharp in focus but the flowers are still so soft. Really a sweet shot!</td>', 'Trading post...  Congratulations on your top ten finish! This is an excellent shot and your processing is fantastic. I love how the rabbit is so sharp in focus but the flowers are still so soft. Really a sweet shot!', '2006-06-07 22:30:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496728, 339857, 2490, '<td valign="top">==Trading Post==<br/> <br/>Trying to catch up from being so far behind...<br/> <br/>Wow, no 1s.  That''s an accomplishment.  That''s an amazing capture, and the pure "difficulty" factor garnered you a lot of high votes.  Your photography has come a LONG ways recently.  The composition here is strong, even though I don''t think I would have cropped it quite this way.</td>', '==Trading Post== Trying to catch up from being so far behind... Wow, no 1s.  That''s an accomplishment.  That''s an amazing capture, and the pure "difficulty" factor garnered you a lot of high votes.  Your photography has come a LONG ways recently.  The composition here is strong, even though I don''t think I would have cropped it quite this way.', '2006-06-07 22:31:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496735, 340445, 2490, '<td valign="top">==Trading Post==<br/> <br/>Wow, a personal best.  I don''t know if the comments are why, but it seems several of the participants are REALLY improving and knocking on the "ribbons" door.  Congratulations on a great score on a great image.</td>', '==Trading Post== Wow, a personal best.  I don''t know if the comments are why, but it seems several of the participants are REALLY improving and knocking on the "ribbons" door.  Congratulations on a great score on a great image.', '2006-06-07 22:32:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496746, 340455, 54283, '<td valign="top">Bautiful, Bautiful shot.<br/></td>', 'Bautiful, Bautiful shot.', '2006-06-07 22:33:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496773, 339214, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Alex!<br/> <br/>Ahh, one of my challenge twins! Congrats on picking such a fine title for your entry ;-)<br/> <br/>I can''t say I don''t like the concept, but I think the sunrises and sunsets probably gave the voters the impression that the entries were shoehorned in. <br/> <br/>From a more technical perspective, it''s a rather dull sunrise, with little texture and color variation in the sky. The buildings along the shore are rather uninteresting, and the pier(?) in the foreground is really distracting.</td>', 'Hi Alex! Ahh, one of my challenge twins! Congrats on picking such a fine title for your entry ;-) I can''t say I don''t like the concept, but I think the sunrises and sunsets probably gave the voters the impression that the entries were shoehorned in.  From a more technical perspective, it''s a rather dull sunrise, with little texture and color variation in the sky. The buildings along the shore are rather uninteresting, and the pier(?) in the foreground is really distracting.', '2006-06-07 22:39:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496786, 340223, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Richard -<br/> <br/>For being a shoehorned entry, you certainly found a good title. Fitting and not overused throughout the field of entries. <br/> <br/>One thing I''ve noticed here is that DPC voters do hate dark, processed images, except when it looks like a draganizer action. We probably have Joey to blame for bringing that style into vogue here.<br/> <br/>Whatever you did put the photo through, it has retained really nice clarity and texture.</td>', 'Hi Richard - For being a shoehorned entry, you certainly found a good title. Fitting and not overused throughout the field of entries.  One thing I''ve noticed here is that DPC voters do hate dark, processed images, except when it looks like a draganizer action. We probably have Joey to blame for bringing that style into vogue here. Whatever you did put the photo through, it has retained really nice clarity and texture.', '2006-06-07 22:43:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496824, 340578, 55642, '<td valign="top">Hi Gunnar -<br/> <br/>I think the frame is what really makes this image interesting. I actually don''t like the processing on it very much, The clouds and the hill are nice and sharp, though verging on looking computer generated. There''s a little hint of oversharpening along the horizon on the left, where there''s a visible halo. The model obviously has been cut into a different layer from the rest of the image, and looks very unnatural - much too sharp and angular - as well as having absolutely no natural texture left. Overall, it looks more like a scene from an online mass-multi or Final Fantasy, which might be cool for a gaming graphic but just does nothing for me as a <i>photograph</i>. <br/> <br/>Perhaps much of that is more taste than tech, since it did have a rather decent finish. Congrats on breaking into the double digits on this one!</td>', 'Hi Gunnar - I think the frame is what really makes this image interesting. I actually don''t like the processing on it very much, The clouds and the hill are nice and sharp, though verging on looking computer generated. There''s a little hint of oversharpening along the horizon on the left, where there''s a visible halo. The model obviously has been cut into a different layer from the rest of the image, and looks very unnatural - much too sharp and angular - as well as having absolutely no natural texture left. Overall, it looks more like a scene from an online mass-multi or Final Fantasy, which might be cool for a gaming graphic but just does nothing for me as a photograph.  Perhaps much of that is more taste than tech, since it did have a rather decent finish. Congrats on breaking into the double digits on this one!', '2006-06-07 22:52:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496841, 340101, 5112, '<td valign="top">Many congratulations on your ribbon with this beautiful image!</td>', 'Many congratulations on your ribbon with this beautiful image!', '2006-06-07 22:56:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496919, 340445, 46448, '<td valign="top">Awesome Shot Kirsty! I love the fact ya did it with some old Glass, all manual! Priceless shot, and brillant!</td>', 'Awesome Shot Kirsty! I love the fact ya did it with some old Glass, all manual! Priceless shot, and brillant!', '2006-06-07 23:17:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496928, 340424, 30982, '<td valign="top">Love the overly "plastic" appearance of the model and her expression is a kick!  Nicely done, and a great interpretation of the challenge.</td>', 'Love the overly "plastic" appearance of the model and her expression is a kick!  Nicely done, and a great interpretation of the challenge.', '2006-06-07 23:21:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496930, 339469, 53147, '<td valign="top">Trading Post - <br/>I voted late on this challenge so I never saw this shot. I will leave the spotlight issue alone. Overall the focus is a bit too soft. Her arm is blown out pretty bad and the lighting on her face seems a bit harsh.  She seems a bit off centered but not quite enough. She looks a bit angry, like I wouldnt want to cross her at that moment. I probably would have scored this a 5 if I had the chance. I hope this didnt com e off too harsh - just my lowly opinion.</td>', 'Trading Post - I voted late on this challenge so I never saw this shot. I will leave the spotlight issue alone. Overall the focus is a bit too soft. Her arm is blown out pretty bad and the lighting on her face seems a bit harsh.  She seems a bit off centered but not quite enough. She looks a bit angry, like I wouldnt want to cross her at that moment. I probably would have scored this a 5 if I had the chance. I hope this didnt com e off too harsh - just my lowly opinion.', '2006-06-07 23:21:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496947, 340450, 30982, '<td valign="top">As a set up shot, this is pretty good and it''s definitely suited to the challenge.  I like the way you used natural light and the shadows it created.  Love the "wallpaper" and the fact you used another picture you''d shot as the view out the window!</td>', 'As a set up shot, this is pretty good and it''s definitely suited to the challenge.  I like the way you used natural light and the shadows it created.  Love the "wallpaper" and the fact you used another picture you''d shot as the view out the window!', '2006-06-07 23:26:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496965, 340761, 30982, '<td valign="top">The clarity in this shot is really amazing.  Overall composition is very good, showing the whole shebang.</td>', 'The clarity in this shot is really amazing.  Overall composition is very good, showing the whole shebang.', '2006-06-07 23:30:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2496987, 339469, 2490, '<td valign="top">==Trading Post==<br/> <br/>The background would have been very plain without the spotlight, so I see why you wanted to add it.  She doesn''t look really happy - perhaps intentional, that''s fine - and the light is glaring a little bit on her forehead.  I DO really like the non-traditionaly prom pose.  Sorry for the DQ :)</td>', '==Trading Post== The background would have been very plain without the spotlight, so I see why you wanted to add it.  She doesn''t look really happy - perhaps intentional, that''s fine - and the light is glaring a little bit on her forehead.  I DO really like the non-traditionaly prom pose.  Sorry for the DQ :)', '2006-06-07 23:37:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497003, 340446, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very appropriate picture for the title!  I like how you left the guy in a fairly good expanse of water to add to the sense of needing help.</td>', 'Very appropriate picture for the title!  I like how you left the guy in a fairly good expanse of water to add to the sense of needing help.', '2006-06-07 23:41:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497069, 340713, 32997, '<td valign="top">I have a soft spot for faces in fishbowls...nice job..</td>', 'I have a soft spot for faces in fishbowls...nice job..', '2006-06-07 23:54:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497093, 340501, 24454, '<td valign="top">Oooooh. . .this IS awesome too!  I just commented on one of your outtakes!   I think either photo would have gotten you the strong score you got here!  I''ve always loved these phantom see-through people in photos.  They look so haunting!</td>', 'Oooooh. . .this IS awesome too!  I just commented on one of your outtakes!   I think either photo would have gotten you the strong score you got here!  I''ve always loved these phantom see-through people in photos.  They look so haunting!', '2006-06-08 00:00:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497095, 339418, 30982, '<td valign="top">This is almost an abstract in a way.  I like the way the light rays show up diagonally and I figure that''s what you were trying to capture.  Hard to catch those!  I suspect part of the lowish score is because there''s no real subject to give the viewer an anchor and perspective.  A tree or church spire or such on the left, with the light angled into it, might have more interest.  Keep shooting!</td>', 'This is almost an abstract in a way.  I like the way the light rays show up diagonally and I figure that''s what you were trying to capture.  Hard to catch those!  I suspect part of the lowish score is because there''s no real subject to give the viewer an anchor and perspective.  A tree or church spire or such on the left, with the light angled into it, might have more interest.  Keep shooting!', '2006-06-08 00:01:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497111, 340552, 30982, '<td valign="top">I was wondering how someone managed to find a submarine!  I like how you used the foliage to frame it and the angle you choosed to shoot from.  Seems to be a bit on the bright side.</td>', 'I was wondering how someone managed to find a submarine!  I like how you used the foliage to frame it and the angle you choosed to shoot from.  Seems to be a bit on the bright side.', '2006-06-08 00:04:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497206, 340595, 36141, '<td valign="top">I''m really amazed how many of the comments are implying that my entry isn''t quite meeting the challenge by saying my road isn''t winding. Why on earth should it be winding???? Can''t you read? I didn''t choose ''a long and winding road'' as my title. You appearently did.</td>', 'I''m really amazed how many of the comments are implying that my entry isn''t quite meeting the challenge by saying my road isn''t winding. Why on earth should it be winding???? Can''t you read? I didn''t choose ''a long and winding road'' as my title. You appearently did.', '2006-06-08 00:29:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497215, 340496, 22734, '<td valign="top">A spectacular rendition to carry away the Blue. Congratulations.</td>', 'A spectacular rendition to carry away the Blue. Congratulations.', '2006-06-08 00:32:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497216, 340101, 22734, '<td valign="top">Beauty and delicasy carries away the moment. Congratulations on your Red.</td>', 'Beauty and delicasy carries away the moment. Congratulations on your Red.', '2006-06-08 00:33:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(2497218, 340294, 22734, '<td valign="top">Simply stunning. Congratulations on your yellow.</td>', 'Simply stunning. Congratulations on your yellow.', '2006-06-08 00:33:49.000000', NULL, 0),
