(2499352, 340639, 33025, '<td valign="top">Oh, one of my favorite songs.<br/>Oddly enough, I haven''t been on DPC in a while, and I was listening to this song just now when I saw the challenge results.<br/>Great photo, excellent use of lighting.</td>', 'Oh, one of my favorite songs.Oddly enough, I haven''t been on DPC in a while, and I was listening to this song just now when I saw the challenge results.Great photo, excellent use of lighting.', '2006-06-08 17:03:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2499380, 338829, 30896, '<td valign="top">Well, i wouldnt say all of the better scoring photos were worse than this one.<br/> <br/>I gave 6 myself since I like the concept and composition, on the other hand it seems noisy (even at ISO 50 which is suprising) and those white lines are quite distracting - were there only concrete w/ the puddle and neat image, I guess it would score higher.</td>', 'Well, i wouldnt say all of the better scoring photos were worse than this one. I gave 6 myself since I like the concept and composition, on the other hand it seems noisy (even at ISO 50 which is suprising) and those white lines are quite distracting - were there only concrete w/ the puddle and neat image, I guess it would score higher.', '2006-06-08 17:12:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2499518, 340101, 18339, '<td valign="top">Very nice!  Congratulations on your ribbon.  I love this image and so creative an idea for the challenge.</td>', 'Very nice!  Congratulations on your ribbon.  I love this image and so creative an idea for the challenge.', '2006-06-08 18:06:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2499749, 340599, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Very nice.  Your subject''s focus is very crisp and he was nicely isolated off the background with a great depth of field.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> Your lighting here looks a little flat and hazy.  I See that you upped the contrast some, but I think it could have used even more.  A slight s curve in curves adjustments would have given this one a great edge.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> While tilted horizons usually drive me nuts, I like this one.  It works well to give the image a nice flow up to your subject.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Nice job meeting the challenge and produce a well-deserved 6+ image.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Very nice.  Your subject''s focus is very crisp and he was nicely isolated off the background with a great depth of field. Lighting: Your lighting here looks a little flat and hazy.  I See that you upped the contrast some, but I think it could have used even more.  A slight s curve in curves adjustments would have given this one a great edge. Composition/Content: While tilted horizons usually drive me nuts, I like this one.  It works well to give the image a nice flow up to your subject. My Opinion: Nice job meeting the challenge and produce a well-deserved 6+ image. Eric', '2006-06-08 19:21:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2499786, 340552, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Great focus, but there is a yellow hue beyond just the yellow of the submarine.  It is more strong at the bottom of the frame.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> You did a nice job with exposure control here, but the shadow at the bottom left of the frame is a bit distracting.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> I think the cropping is just a bit too tight.  You need just a little more space between the submarine and the left side of the frame.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Wonderful job meeting the challenge.  Coming across a yellow submarine was a great find.  With a few slight adjustments, this one surely would have pulled a much better score.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Great focus, but there is a yellow hue beyond just the yellow of the submarine.  It is more strong at the bottom of the frame. Lighting: You did a nice job with exposure control here, but the shadow at the bottom left of the frame is a bit distracting. Composition/Content: I think the cropping is just a bit too tight.  You need just a little more space between the submarine and the left side of the frame. My Opinion: Wonderful job meeting the challenge.  Coming across a yellow submarine was a great find.  With a few slight adjustments, this one surely would have pulled a much better score. Eric', '2006-06-08 19:33:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2499808, 339696, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>Hey there from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Everything looks pretty well focused here, but there are some very strong textures in this one that you could have brought out even more.  With a little more contrast, this one could have been even more appealing.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> I like the lighting.  Everything looks very evenly lit, but just a touch flat.  Upping the contrast would also remedy that look.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Very well composed.  I have to disagree with the comment by docvorhies.  I think that there is tones of interest there, and getting closer would add to that even more.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> Fine job meeting the challenge.  With some slight adjustments, this one would have scored even better.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', 'Hey there from the Critique Club  Camera Work/Technical: Everything looks pretty well focused here, but there are some very strong textures in this one that you could have brought out even more.  With a little more contrast, this one could have been even more appealing. Lighting: I like the lighting.  Everything looks very evenly lit, but just a touch flat.  Upping the contrast would also remedy that look. Composition/Content: Very well composed.  I have to disagree with the comment by docvorhies.  I think that there is tones of interest there, and getting closer would add to that even more. My Opinion: Fine job meeting the challenge.  With some slight adjustments, this one would have scored even better. Eric', '2006-06-08 19:43:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2499990, 340445, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>--Trading Post Comment--</b> <br/> <br/>Well, I think we all knew that it was only a matter of time.  Much of your portfolio is terrific, and breaking into the top ten was only a matter of time.  You did a great job in meeting the challenge, as well as producing a technically superb image.  I am not using my normal critique flow becasue there are not many things I would suggest changing.  I would ask that you include your editing steps in the Photographer''s Comments.  It really helps out when I critique an image.  The only technical change I would make would be adding a curves adjustment to reduce some of the haze in the shot.  A slight s-curve would have done this, adding a bit of contrast as well.  Nice work, and congrats on a well-deserved top 10!</td>', '--Trading Post Comment--  Well, I think we all knew that it was only a matter of time.  Much of your portfolio is terrific, and breaking into the top ten was only a matter of time.  You did a great job in meeting the challenge, as well as producing a technically superb image.  I am not using my normal critique flow becasue there are not many things I would suggest changing.  I would ask that you include your editing steps in the Photographer''s Comments.  It really helps out when I critique an image.  The only technical change I would make would be adding a curves adjustment to reduce some of the haze in the shot.  A slight s-curve would have done this, adding a bit of contrast as well.  Nice work, and congrats on a well-deserved top 10!', '2006-06-08 21:00:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2500021, 339857, 36065, '<td valign="top"><b>--Trading Post Comment--</b> <br/> <br/>First of all, congrats on your best scoring photograph to date.  I would encourage you to include your post-processing in the Photographer''s Comments along with the great info that you''ve already included.<br/> <br/><b>Camera Work/Technical:</b> Great, crisp focus and a nice job keeping the entire scene in focus.<br/> <br/><b>Lighting:</b> The lighting is very even.  I think I am reading that you used the on camera flash.  If that is indeed the case, you did a fine job with it.<br/> <br/><b>Composition/Content:</b> Not bad, but I think that a portrait style crop might have worked better than the landscape.  I find myself wanting to see the bottom of the nest.<br/> <br/><b>My Opinion:</b> This is a very nice image and a well-deserved top 15 finish.  I think that I would have used a white border and shot it in portrait orientation.  I think this one would have broken 7 with those two changes.<br/> <br/>Eric<br/></td>', '--Trading Post Comment--  First of all, congrats on your best scoring photograph to date.  I would encourage you to include your post-processing in the Photographer''s Comments along with the great info that you''ve already included. Camera Work/Technical: Great, crisp focus and a nice job keeping the entire scene in focus. Lighting: The lighting is very even.  I think I am reading that you used the on camera flash.  If that is indeed the case, you did a fine job with it. Composition/Content: Not bad, but I think that a portrait style crop might have worked better than the landscape.  I find myself wanting to see the bottom of the nest. My Opinion: This is a very nice image and a well-deserved top 15 finish.  I think that I would have used a white border and shot it in portrait orientation.  I think this one would have broken 7 with those two changes. Eric', '2006-06-08 21:11:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(2500025, 340599, 14837, '<td valign="top">Eric, thank you for the wonderful critique.<br/> <br/>I know it looks a bit flat... I decided to drop the saturation on this photo... it didn''t speak to me in the same way as the fully contrasted one.  <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=345300" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14837/thumb/345300.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14837/thumb/345300.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/14837/thumb/345300.jpg"/></a> <br/></td>', 'Eric, thank you for the wonderful critique. I know it looks a bit flat... I decided to drop the saturation on this photo... it didn''t speak to me in the same way as the fully contrasted one.    ', '2006-06-08 21:13:31.000000', NULL, 0),
