(2511893, 340509, 13547, '<td valign="top">Aaww this is fantastic!  I love the song too so it certainly appeals to me.  This challenge certainly brought out the best in lots of people!</td>', 'Aaww this is fantastic!  I love the song too so it certainly appeals to me.  This challenge certainly brought out the best in lots of people!', '2006-06-13 06:46:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2511895, 339281, 13547, '<td valign="top">Well done Dad - now I know where I get my knack for terrible puns from!</td>', 'Well done Dad - now I know where I get my knack for terrible puns from!', '2006-06-13 06:49:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2512260, 339413, 39007, '<td valign="top">I"m one of the ones who gave you a low score - you have asked for comments so I''ll try to explain. Bear in mind this is entirely my opnion and of course others opinions will vary.<br/> <br/>The biggest problem in my opinion is lack of focus. It makes it hard to appreciate the photo when I''m not even sure what the subject is - the background could be trees but I''m not certain. The blue object could be a ribbon but again its not clear. Its a very rare photo that works well for me when everything is blurry.<br/> <br/>Apart from this I cannot link the image to the title. The blue is clearly not the sky or sea, and the green doesn''t look like a sea. Neither particularly remind me of sea or sky either. This was enough to make me feel the image did not meet the challenge well.<br/> <br/>Really its quite an abstract image and its rare for an abstract to be voted high here. Personally I like artwork to work on a basic literal level as well as higher levels... <br/> <br/>I hope this helps.</td>', 'I"m one of the ones who gave you a low score - you have asked for comments so I''ll try to explain. Bear in mind this is entirely my opnion and of course others opinions will vary. The biggest problem in my opinion is lack of focus. It makes it hard to appreciate the photo when I''m not even sure what the subject is - the background could be trees but I''m not certain. The blue object could be a ribbon but again its not clear. Its a very rare photo that works well for me when everything is blurry. Apart from this I cannot link the image to the title. The blue is clearly not the sky or sea, and the green doesn''t look like a sea. Neither particularly remind me of sea or sky either. This was enough to make me feel the image did not meet the challenge well. Really its quite an abstract image and its rare for an abstract to be voted high here. Personally I like artwork to work on a basic literal level as well as higher levels...  I hope this helps.', '2006-06-13 10:06:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2512481, 339413, 34659, '<td valign="top">Ya know...  I almost used the exact same verse.  And I remember this shot very well from the challenge.  (I also have a brown ribbon - as do a number of other fairly well respected photogs on here, so wear it proudly, I do!)<br/> <br/>I scored this a 5.  I personally liked the filter(s) you used, but was afraid you''d get *hit* for it by voters who didn''t stop long enough to really look at the shot.  Many people will just glance and think it''s out of focus, rather than seeing that it''s made to be more abstract or like a watercolor painting, mimicking the words and meaning of the song lyrics (at least that''s my take on it).<br/> <br/>What do I think could improve this?: The lighting is harsh on the ribbon - you''ve got some nice shadow play, but the brightness against the rest of the rather dull image is a little too much.  The colors could be much brighter and *happier*.  We''re talking about a sea of green and a sky of blue in someone''s imagination, so the colors could almost be surreally bright and/or unusual (but usually not drab).<br/> <br/>Again, I think you had a great idea and I think you were on the right track with the filter idea, it just didn''t quite translate or convey the best that it could have.  Keep at it and I still think you do some very interesting and creative things.  I''m looking forward to seeing more!</td>', 'Ya know...  I almost used the exact same verse.  And I remember this shot very well from the challenge.  (I also have a brown ribbon - as do a number of other fairly well respected photogs on here, so wear it proudly, I do!) I scored this a 5.  I personally liked the filter(s) you used, but was afraid you''d get *hit* for it by voters who didn''t stop long enough to really look at the shot.  Many people will just glance and think it''s out of focus, rather than seeing that it''s made to be more abstract or like a watercolor painting, mimicking the words and meaning of the song lyrics (at least that''s my take on it). What do I think could improve this?: The lighting is harsh on the ribbon - you''ve got some nice shadow play, but the brightness against the rest of the rather dull image is a little too much.  The colors could be much brighter and *happier*.  We''re talking about a sea of green and a sky of blue in someone''s imagination, so the colors could almost be surreally bright and/or unusual (but usually not drab). Again, I think you had a great idea and I think you were on the right track with the filter idea, it just didn''t quite translate or convey the best that it could have.  Keep at it and I still think you do some very interesting and creative things.  I''m looking forward to seeing more!', '2006-06-13 11:42:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2512587, 338809, 40465, '<td valign="top">Hi!<br/> <br/>I love the clouds! Drama is the perfect way to descrive it.  Its as if the sun is coming to rescue us:)<br/> <br/>The water on the right is a bit dark, otherwise great shot:)</td>', 'Hi! I love the clouds! Drama is the perfect way to descrive it.  Its as if the sun is coming to rescue us:) The water on the right is a bit dark, otherwise great shot:)', '2006-06-13 12:21:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(2513199, 338809, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club. <br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Very Nice cloud shot. <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Someone gave me a tip that the horizon should be on third for this kind of images. I found the tip very useful, try it and let me know if you found it useful too.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Very nice. I always like the sunrise/sunset pictures with coulds. <br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>The exposure is bit tricky here. The right most is bit dark, but if you try to increase the exposure some area will be blown out. Try using exposure lock for this kind of pictures. <br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>Horizon at third, and exposure to give details on the right side.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Really like the image as is, but may score even higher with bit improvement IMO.<br/> <br/>Cheers!! Keep shooting.</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club.  First Impression Very Nice cloud shot. Composition: Someone gave me a tip that the horizon should be on third for this kind of images. I found the tip very useful, try it and let me know if you found it useful too.Subject: Very nice. I always like the sunrise/sunset pictures with coulds. Technical (Colour and light): The exposure is bit tricky here. The right most is bit dark, but if you try to increase the exposure some area will be blown out. Try using exposure lock for this kind of pictures. Improvement: Horizon at third, and exposure to give details on the right side.Summary: Really like the image as is, but may score even higher with bit improvement IMO. Cheers!! Keep shooting.', '2006-06-13 15:50:09.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(2513843, 340294, 58047, '<td valign="top">A gorgeous snowscape and the clouds really add to the shot aswell, Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'A gorgeous snowscape and the clouds really add to the shot aswell, Congrats on the ribbon.', '2006-06-13 20:30:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2514304, 338767, 30982, '<td valign="top">Forget "wow''ing" the DPC crowd - some of us like what you do just the way you do it and are pretty darn impressed with stuff like this.</td>', 'Forget "wow''ing" the DPC crowd - some of us like what you do just the way you do it and are pretty darn impressed with stuff like this.', '2006-06-13 23:44:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2514557, 340196, 10818, '<td valign="top">Its a wonderful shot Brad, very cool.<br/> <br/>Congrats on quitting smoking, wish you the best !</td>', 'Its a wonderful shot Brad, very cool. Congrats on quitting smoking, wish you the best !', '2006-06-14 00:57:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2516153, 339857, 50551, '<td valign="top">Post Challenge Critique...<br/>Challenge: Beatles Song/Lyrics (Advanced Editing)<br/>Challenge Description: too lazy to cut and paste this :-(<br/> <br/>A Score re meeting the challenge<br/>{ 0} Does not meet challenge<br/>{+1} Clearly meets the challenge<br/>**{+2} Epitomises the idea behind the challenge<br/>I know the track so this is right in line with the challenge and the sentiments of the original song.<br/> <br/>B Composition &amp; Aesthetics<br/>{ 0} No discernible compositional form or merit<br/>{+1} Snap-shot like composition<br/>**{+2} Well composed, aesthetically pleasing<br/>{+3} An exceptional composition/exceptional aesthetics<br/>It is all in this shot: leading lines, rule of thirds and emotion. There is a narrative to the picture, too.<br/> <br/>C Technical Considerations<br/>{ 0} Technically flawed<br/>{+1} Technically OK<br/>**{+2} Technically well executed<br/>{+3} Evidence of technical mastery/wizardry<br/>There is a potential lack of detail in the neck and head area of the chicks that is not helped by the shadow that underpins most of them. Maybe you do need that new flash and the use of something like a LightSphere, a diffuser or maybe just bouncing the flash to soften the shadows. But this is nit-picking as the rest hangs together well.<br/> <br/>D WOW Factor<br/>{ 0} Not special/ordinary<br/>{+1} Has some degree of impact<br/>**{+2} Obvious impact<br/>{+3} Slaps you in face <br/>This one really hits home as there is so much character in the picture. Almost a slap :-)<br/> <br/>Total score: 8<br/></td>', 'Post Challenge Critique...Challenge: Beatles Song/Lyrics (Advanced Editing)Challenge Description: too lazy to cut and paste this :-( A Score re meeting the challenge{ 0} Does not meet challenge{+1} Clearly meets the challenge**{+2} Epitomises the idea behind the challengeI know the track so this is right in line with the challenge and the sentiments of the original song. B Composition & Aesthetics{ 0} No discernible compositional form or merit{+1} Snap-shot like composition**{+2} Well composed, aesthetically pleasing{+3} An exceptional composition/exceptional aestheticsIt is all in this shot: leading lines, rule of thirds and emotion. There is a narrative to the picture, too. C Technical Considerations{ 0} Technically flawed{+1} Technically OK**{+2} Technically well executed{+3} Evidence of technical mastery/wizardryThere is a potential lack of detail in the neck and head area of the chicks that is not helped by the shadow that underpins most of them. Maybe you do need that new flash and the use of something like a LightSphere, a diffuser or maybe just bouncing the flash to soften the shadows. But this is nit-picking as the rest hangs together well. D WOW Factor{ 0} Not special/ordinary{+1} Has some degree of impact**{+2} Obvious impact{+3} Slaps you in face This one really hits home as there is so much character in the picture. Almost a slap :-) Total score: 8', '2006-06-14 10:50:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2517265, 340534, 36060, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your kind comments and votes - much appreciated!</td>', 'Thank you all for your kind comments and votes - much appreciated!', '2006-06-14 16:54:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2517728, 340534, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is stunning. I think it should be a top 5 for sure!</td>', 'This is stunning. I think it should be a top 5 for sure!', '2006-06-14 18:54:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2518356, 340554, 51538, '<td valign="top">Regardless of the Beatles connection, this is a very fine image which I find pleasing to look at more than once.</td>', 'Regardless of the Beatles connection, this is a very fine image which I find pleasing to look at more than once.', '2006-06-14 22:35:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2518628, 338809, 38496, '<td valign="top">hi from ctp2:<br/> <br/>This is a lovely image.  I really like the clouds in this, and the water is a gorgeous color through most of the picture.  Two things that worked against you here (imho) - the bottom right corner is sort of dark, and the idea that the sun is coming out is sort of subtle.  This would have done better as "here comes the storm".  Still a really pretty shot, though.</td>', 'hi from ctp2: This is a lovely image.  I really like the clouds in this, and the water is a gorgeous color through most of the picture.  Two things that worked against you here (imho) - the bottom right corner is sort of dark, and the idea that the sun is coming out is sort of subtle.  This would have done better as "here comes the storm".  Still a really pretty shot, though.', '2006-06-15 00:04:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2518694, 339214, 38496, '<td valign="top">hi from ctp2:<br/> <br/>Hi Alex,<br/>  This is a ''nice'' shot, but super ''grabbing'' if that makes sense.  The colors are pretty, but something about it is a little distracting.  Nothing really stands out, except maybe the pier, which isn''t really the focus of the picture.  I like the sky and the cityscape quite a bit, though.</td>', 'hi from ctp2: Hi Alex,  This is a ''nice'' shot, but super ''grabbing'' if that makes sense.  The colors are pretty, but something about it is a little distracting.  Nothing really stands out, except maybe the pier, which isn''t really the focus of the picture.  I like the sky and the cityscape quite a bit, though.', '2006-06-15 00:20:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2518709, 340223, 38496, '<td valign="top">hi from ctp2:<br/> <br/>Another good finish!  This fit the challenge nicely, and is also a nice candid.  The reflection in the glass right behind the man is a little distracting.  I really like the lighting, though, and the way the man''s white shirt contrasts with the dark surroundings.</td>', 'hi from ctp2: Another good finish!  This fit the challenge nicely, and is also a nice candid.  The reflection in the glass right behind the man is a little distracting.  I really like the lighting, though, and the way the man''s white shirt contrasts with the dark surroundings.', '2006-06-15 00:25:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519739, 340303, 43410, '<td valign="top">thanks so much to all the great comments.  i learned a lot from this challenge.  thanks again :)</td>', 'thanks so much to all the great comments.  i learned a lot from this challenge.  thanks again :)', '2006-06-15 10:21:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(2519749, 338809, 42125, '<td valign="top"><b>CTCP2 Gunnsi<br/>First impression:</b> <br/>Good looking stormy clouds. Not a sun coming up but a disappearing sun. The picture is in focus and there is this beautiful red colour but not enough.<br/><b>What can you do better?</b> <br/>I think what is wrong is how you build this image. To heavy on one side while there is nothing on the other. To bright on one side and to dark on the other. You could IMO have just zoomed in on the red sky at the horizon.<br/>I hope there will be no plaque on my house for I gave this picture only 4.</td>', 'CTCP2 GunnsiFirst impression: Good looking stormy clouds. Not a sun coming up but a disappearing sun. The picture is in focus and there is this beautiful red colour but not enough.What can you do better? I think what is wrong is how you build this image. To heavy on one side while there is nothing on the other. To bright on one side and to dark on the other. You could IMO have just zoomed in on the red sky at the horizon.I hope there will be no plaque on my house for I gave this picture only 4.', '2006-06-15 10:25:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2521558, 340196, 23394, '<td valign="top">i''m too tired from thinking about the climb to really enjoy the photo ;-)</td>', 'i''m too tired from thinking about the climb to really enjoy the photo ;-)', '2006-06-15 23:23:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522083, 340424, 59501, '<td valign="top">Hilarious! She''s really made up--look at those lashes! I like all the bright colors.</td>', 'Hilarious! She''s really made up--look at those lashes! I like all the bright colors.', '2006-06-16 08:34:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522425, 339214, 42125, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2 Gunnsi<br/>First impression</b> <br/>Beautiful sunrise (or sunset). Good colours, lack of details and a tractor in the foreground.<br/><b>What can you do better</b> <br/>IMO there is to much empty space above the sun, a different crop would have helped there. Stand in a place where there are no distracting things like a tractor in the foreground. Zoom a bit more in so that there will be more details in the houses.</td>', 'Greetings from CTP2 GunnsiFirst impression Beautiful sunrise (or sunset). Good colours, lack of details and a tractor in the foreground.What can you do better IMO there is to much empty space above the sun, a different crop would have helped there. Stand in a place where there are no distracting things like a tractor in the foreground. Zoom a bit more in so that there will be more details in the houses.', '2006-06-16 12:21:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522461, 340631, 42125, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2 Gunnsi<br/>First impression</b> <br/>You met the challenge but this picture only shows strawberries but not a field. Good looking strawberries and some of them in superb focus and show a great detail. Lovely colours. This picture would have scored well in the Bokeh challenge I think.<br/><b>What can you do better</b> <br/>The picture is maybe a bit too simple. Adding something to the strawberries might have helped. There is nothing that connects this to the Beatles but the title. (the same for my picture).<br/>I saw this thread two days ago, read''em and weep :-)<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=156130&amp;page=3" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Win a Ribbon</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-06-16 11:38:38.</i></td>', 'Greetings from CTP2 GunnsiFirst impression You met the challenge but this picture only shows strawberries but not a field. Good looking strawberries and some of them in superb focus and show a great detail. Lovely colours. This picture would have scored well in the Bokeh challenge I think.What can you do better The picture is maybe a bit too simple. Adding something to the strawberries might have helped. There is nothing that connects this to the Beatles but the title. (the same for my picture).I saw this thread two days ago, read''em and weep :-)Win a Ribbon', '2006-06-16 12:36:03.000000', '2006-06-16 12:38:38.000000', 0),
(2522534, 340223, 42125, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from CTP2 Gunnsi<br/>First impression</b> <br/>You met the challenge and still going within top 20.<br/>Good picture of a tired man. You met the challenge. Good focus, good placement/angle and rules of thirds. This is a beautiful benche (seat) and that gives you some points.<br/><b>What can you do better</b> <br/>Ask him to move his left foot a bit :-) it sort of hangs there.<br/>Sorry I can''t give you any suggestions on making this better.</td>', 'Greetings from CTP2 GunnsiFirst impression You met the challenge and still going within top 20.Good picture of a tired man. You met the challenge. Good focus, good placement/angle and rules of thirds. This is a beautiful benche (seat) and that gives you some points.What can you do better Ask him to move his left foot a bit :-) it sort of hangs there.Sorry I can''t give you any suggestions on making this better.', '2006-06-16 13:13:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2522654, 339214, 30454, '<td valign="top">Greetings from your own critique club.<br/> <br/><b>First Impression</b> <br/>Very Nice Sunrise shot. <br/><b>Composition:</b> <br/>Nice composition. I like the horizon following rule of third.<br/><b>Subject:</b> <br/>Nice choice of subject for the challenge. If I am not wrong there are other couple of entriies with the same theme.<br/><b>Technical (Colour and light):</b> <br/>Colors and light is perfect for this one. <br/><b>Improvement:</b> <br/>The hallo around the Sun and the on the edge of the building needs to be avoided. Don''t know if the hallo is due to PP or it was there in the original.<br/><b>Summary:</b> <br/>Nice sunrise picture, would have scores high with just little improvement.<br/> <br/>Cheers!! Keep shooting.</td>', 'Greetings from your own critique club. First Impression Very Nice Sunrise shot. Composition: Nice composition. I like the horizon following rule of third.Subject: Nice choice of subject for the challenge. If I am not wrong there are other couple of entriies with the same theme.Technical (Colour and light): Colors and light is perfect for this one. Improvement: The hallo around the Sun and the on the edge of the building needs to be avoided. Don''t know if the hallo is due to PP or it was there in the original.Summary: Nice sunrise picture, would have scores high with just little improvement. Cheers!! Keep shooting.', '2006-06-16 14:26:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(2523093, 338767, 23430, '<td valign="top">This has got perfect focus for such a difficult shot and the background is great. The composition is spot on and her expression is nice and interesting. I bet she loves this shot. Except for the slight lack of light on her face this is an all round perfect shot and one of the most underated shots I''ve seen in a challenge. This is the sought of shot I like to take. Maybe you should have had someone tossing up diamonds in the background. Better luck in the sports challenge eh.</td>', 'This has got perfect focus for such a difficult shot and the background is great. The composition is spot on and her expression is nice and interesting. I bet she loves this shot. Except for the slight lack of light on her face this is an all round perfect shot and one of the most underated shots I''ve seen in a challenge. This is the sought of shot I like to take. Maybe you should have had someone tossing up diamonds in the background. Better luck in the sports challenge eh.', '2006-06-16 18:32:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(2523906, 338767, 35357, '<td valign="top">Totally sweet!</td>', 'Totally sweet!', '2006-06-17 09:29:55.000000', NULL, 0),
